---
import LinkCards from '../components/LinkCards.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { fetchContributors } from '../lib/github';

const repo = 'https://github.com/tachyon-cms/tachyoncms';
const contributors = await fetchContributors();
---

<Base
  title="Community · TachyonCMS"
  description="Where to ask, how to contribute, and the promises that keep TachyonCMS open: MIT, no CLA, sign-off under the DCO."
  path="/community"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Community"
    title="Small enough that one pull request changes it"
    lede="TachyonCMS is built in public, on GitHub. Questions, ideas, bug reports and code all land in the same place, and every decision is made where you can read it."
  />

  <div class="community">
    <section aria-labelledby="talk">
      <Prose><h2 id="talk">Where to talk</h2></Prose>
      <LinkCards
        links={[
          {
            href: `${repo}/discussions`,
            title: 'Discussions',
            text: 'Questions, ideas, and the polls that set the roadmap.',
          },
          { href: `${repo}/issues/new/choose`, title: 'Open an issue', text: 'Found a bug? Tell us how to make it happen.' },
          {
            href: `${repo}/security/advisories/new`,
            title: 'Report a vulnerability',
            text: "Privately, never in a public issue. Email security@tachyoncms.com if you can't use GitHub.",
          },
        ]}
      />
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="contribute">
      <Prose>
        <h2 id="contribute">Contributing</h2>
        <p>
          Start with a <a href={`${repo}/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aopen+label%3A%22good+first+issue%22`}>good first issue</a
          >. Each one says which files to change, how to test it, and when it's done. Say you're taking it on the issue,
          and it's yours. Small fixes (a typo, a doc, an obvious bug) can go straight to a pull request. For anything
          bigger, open an issue or a discussion first, so nobody spends a weekend on something that clashes with the
          roadmap.
        </p>
        <p>
          Rust helps for most of the code. It isn't needed for docs and copy, and those fixes count just as much.{' '}
          <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>CONTRIBUTING.md</a> takes you from clone to merged pull request.
        </p>
      </Prose>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="promises">
      <Prose>
        <h2 id="promises">What won't change</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>It stays open source,</strong> under the MIT License.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>No CLA, ever, and no copyright assignment.</strong> You keep the copyright to your work and sign off
            each commit under the <a href="https://developercertificate.org/">Developer Certificate of Origin</a> with{' '}
            <code>git commit -s</code>. Because copyright stays with everyone who contributed, no single person or company
            can take the project closed.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Sponsors get visibility, not control.</strong> Every feature lives in the open source project, and
            nobody can pay to have one held back from everyone else.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          While the project is small, I make the final call, in public. Anyone who contributes steadily and reviews other
          people's work can be invited to become a maintainer, and once maintainers come from more than one organization,
          the plan is to move the project, its trademark and its domains to a neutral foundation. It's all in{' '}
          <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/GOVERNANCE.md`}>GOVERNANCE.md</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          The <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md`}>Code of Conduct</a> applies everywhere in the project. Report
          a problem to <a href="mailto:conduct@tachyoncms.com">conduct@tachyoncms.com</a>. Thinking of sponsoring? Write
          to <a href="mailto:sponsors@tachyoncms.com">sponsors@tachyoncms.com</a>.
        </p>
      </Prose>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="people">
      <Prose>
        <h2 id="people">Contributors</h2>
        <p>Everyone with a commit on <code>main</code>, most commits first. The next name could be yours.</p>
      </Prose>
      <ul class="people">
        {
          contributors.map((c) => (
            <li>
              <a href={c.url}>@{c.login}</a>
              <span>
                {c.contributions} {c.contributions === 1 ? 'commit' : 'commits'}
              </span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .community {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    padding-bottom: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 5rem);
  }
  .community :global(.prose h2) {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .people {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .people li {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.2rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--c-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--c-border);
    border-radius: 14px;
  }
  .people a {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .people span {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--c-muted);
  }
</style>
